'''R4-P17''', nicknamed '''R4''', was a brave but cautious [[Gender|feminine]] [[R4-P Astromech|R4-P]] [[astromech droid]] that was assigned to [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], prior to and throughout the [[Clone Wars]]. She was destroyed by a [[Pistoeka sabotage droid|buzz droid]] during the [[Battle of Coruscant]].

==Biography==
===Separatist Crisis===
[[File:R4-P17-SWZ.png|thumb|right|270px|R4-P17 in the droid socket of Kenobi's starfighter]]
R4-P17 was manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]] sometime prior to the Clone Wars.<ref name="Ultimate" /> A model of the [[R4-P Astromech|R4-P]]<ref name="Guardians of the Republic" /> sub-line of the [[R4 astromech droid|R4 astromech]],<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> the [[Gender|feminine]]<ref name="Ultimate" /> [[astromech droid]] [[Mission to Kamino (Separatist Crisis)|accompanied]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] to [[Kamino]] and [[Geonosis]] as the [[Jedi]] sought to uncover the mysteries behind the [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala|assassination attempts]] on [[Naboo (people)|Naboo]] [[senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] that occurred on the [[The galaxy|galactic]] [[capital]] [[Coruscant]].<ref name="AOTC" />

===The Clone Wars===
====Tatooine====
[[File:R4-P17_zaps_Jawa.png|thumb|left|270px|R4 protects Kenobi's starfighter from Jawas.]]
R4 continued to serve Obi-Wan during the Clone Wars, after gaining an Astromech Body to roam around outside of the [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's Delta-7B Aethersprite-class light interceptor|Jedi starfighter]]. She accompanied her master to the planet [[Tatooine]] to negotiate with [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure]]. At one point, [[Jawa]]s approached Obi-Wan Kenobi's starfighter as R4 was standing in the droid socket, waiting for him to return. She electrocuted one of the Jawas to defend herself and the starfighter and they left. She later traveled to the planet [[Teth]] with her master to assist [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Ahsoka Tano]] in [[Battle of Teth|rescuing Jabba's son]], piloting Obi-Wan Kenobi's starfighter after he jumped from it to fight in the battle on the surface of the planet.<ref name="TCW film" />

====Rodia====
R4 was roaming the halls of the temple and, later on, travelled with Obi-Wan Kenobi to [[Rodia]] to prevent the [[Bounty hunter|bounty hunter]] [[Cad Bane]] from abducting [[Wee Dunn]].<ref name="Children of the Force>{{TCW|Children of the Force}}</ref>

====Mandalore====
[[File:R4P17-SWCT.png|thumb|right|200px|R4-P17 during the Clone Wars]]
R4 traveled to the planet [[Mandalore]] with her master to discuss an [[Attack on a Republic cruiser]] with [[Satine Kryze]]. R4 was left behind while her master travelled to [[Sundari Royal Palace]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot">{{TCW|The Mandalore Plot}}</ref>

====Battle of Sullust====
R4 participated in the [[Battle of Sullust]], during which she and her master were shot down by [[Asajj Ventress]]. The pair escaped when the Command ship was destroyed.<ref name="Nightsisters">{{TCW|Nightsisters (episode)}}</ref>

===Jedi Temple===
R4 was present, alongside [[R4-M1]] in one of the corridors of the [[Jedi Temple]] as Obi-Wan Kenobi and [[Mace Windu]] were discussing [[Yoda]].<ref name="Voices">{{TCW|Voices}}</ref>

===Destruction===
{{Quote|Oh, dear.|Obi-Wan Kenobi comments on R4's destruction|<ref name="ROTS" />}}
[[File:R4-P17_Buzz_Droids.png|thumb|left|270px|R4-P17 during the Battle of Coruscant]]
During the final days of the Clone Wars, R4-P17 joined Obi-Wan Kenobi once again aboard his [[Eta-2 Actis-class light interceptor|Eta-2 ''Actis''-class light interceptor]] in a [[Battle of Coruscant|battle above Coruscant]]. During the battle, [[Jedi Knight]]s Obi-Wan Kenobi and [[Anakin Skywalker]] approached [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[General]] [[Grievous]]' [[flagship]], the ''[[Invisible Hand]]'', in an attempt to rescue the kidnapped [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]]. As the two Jedi neared the flagship, they were attacked by [[Vulture-class starfighter|vulture droids]] that launched [[discord missile]]s at the pair. While Anakin managed to trick the missiles into destroying themselves, Kenobi could not, resulting in them unleashing a payload of [[Pistoeka sabotage droid|buzz droids]] that landed on his starfighter. Kenobi warned R4-P17 to be careful, but by that time, the buzz droids had already sawed<ref name="ROTS" /> her<ref name="Ultimate" /> dome off, destroying her.<ref name="ROTS" />

She was later replaced by [[R4-G9]] as Kenobi's companion [[droid]] during his travel to the [[planet]] [[Utapau]].<ref name="ROTS" />

[[Standard decade|Decade]]s later, a picture of R4 in [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's Eta-2 Actis-class interceptor]] was in the ''[[Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'', a survival guide written by [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and [[DK-RA-43]].<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref>

==Personality and traits==
R4 was an [[R4-P Astromech|R4-P]]<ref name="Guardians of the Republic" /> [[astromech droid]]<ref name="AOTC" /> with [[Gender|feminine programming]]<ref name="Ultimate" /> who stood at 0.96 [[meter]]s (3 [[Foot|feet]], 2 inches) tall. She sported a red replacement dome from another astromech droid<ref name="Join the Battle" /> and had an [[electro-shock prod]].<ref name="TCW film" /> She was brave and had quick reflexes, acting instantly and expertly when Jawas attempted to attack her<ref name="TCW film" /> as well as during the [[Dogfight over Geonosis|fight]] against [[Slave I]]<ref name="AOTC" />, the [[Battle of Teth]]<ref name="TCW film" /> and the [[Battle of Coruscant]].<ref name="ROTS" /> Her bravery was also evident throughout the Clone Wars as she fought against the Separatists.<ref name="Ultimate" /> She was also cautious, making her a great companion for Obi-Wan Kenobi.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Skills and abilities==
{{Quote|R4, prepare to jettison spare part canisters.|Obi-Wan Kenobi to R4-P17|<ref name="AOTC" />}}
As a product of Industrial Automaton, R4 was designed to qualify as a [[hyperspace]] navigator to calculate [[lightspeed]] jumps. She was also an engineer for repair and maintenance.<ref name="Ultimate" /> and was effective at information retrieval and, as well as a good starfighter pilot.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Equipment==
[[File:R4P17-TCWCEJtB.png|thumb|270px|R4-P17 and her multitudinous tools]]
R4 had an electro-shock prod, which she used to protect Kenobi's [[Delta-7B Aethersprite-class light interceptor|Delta-7B ''Aethersprite''-class light interceptor]] from [[Jawa]]s during a visit to Jabba's Palace.<ref name="TCW film" />

==Behind the scenes==
R4-P17 first appeared in the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], the second installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[prequel trilogy]].<ref name="AOTC" />

